. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Model: linear OLS regression
.         
.         * We use the variable inc_share (generated above) as a measure of gen
> der equality in the household. 
.         * If the woman earns a larger share of the total household income, th
> is is a behavioral measure of more gender equality.
.         
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with inc_share
>  as dependent variable and the dummy variable kidsex01 as independent variabl
> e,
.         * additionally controlling for the birth year of each partner.
. 
.         
.         reg inc_share kidsex01 gebjahr_f gebjahr_m if sex==2, cluster(hid) 

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =     37,549
                                                F(3, 5815)        =       1.18
                                                Prob > F          =     0.3160
                                                R-squared         =     0.0025
                                                Root MSE          =     .18812

